## Part 1: bbff534 (the Windows lane's unreviewed DST commit, merged as 8923bc0)
bbff534 fix(limitParser): resolve a DST fall-back repeated hour to the later instant
nextZonedOccurrence's 2-pass convergence always anchored on the offset in
effect at the naively-guessed instant, which is always the EARLIER of the
two real instants that share a repeated wall-clock reading during a fall-back
transition (verified by direct execution: America/Chicago 2026-11-01
01:30am resolved to 06:30Z/CDT, not 07:30Z/CST). Detect the ambiguity by
checking whether stepping the candidate forward an hour still reads the same
wall clock, and prefer that later instant: waking an hour late finds a
still-live limit safe to re-check, waking an hour early risks resuming into
a session that has not actually reset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


